repository-code: "<https://github.com/<user>/<repo>>"
abstract: >-
  A controlled, CPU-only case study measuring how training-corpus specialization
  changes byte-level BPE tokenizer compression on unseen Azure, other Microsoft,
  external technical (Kubernetes), and general-English documentation. Under a
  fixed 32 MiB byte-matched training budget and matched 16K vocabulary, an
  Azure-trained tokenizer used 36.68% fewer tokens per 1,000 UTF-8 bytes than a
  general-English tokenizer on a cross-service Azure holdout, with a general-
  English regression and a mixed-corpus tradeoff. Measures tokenization only; no
  model-quality, latency, or cost claims.
keywords:
  - tokenization
  - byte-level BPE
  - domain adaptation
  - text compression
  - technical documentation
  - reproducible research
